Interest Accrual and Timing of Late Payment Fees
Interest and Early Repayments
Interest on the Loan is calculated on a flat rate basis as disclosed under Clause 7.5.3. Notwithstanding any early repayment of the Loan (in whole or in part) prior to the due date, interest shall accrue and be payable on the outstanding Loan amount for the full term up to and including the original due date, including any period of advance payment. For clarity, such interest shall be calculated as if the Loan remained fully outstanding through the original due date. The full interest amount will be displayed in your Account on the App at the time of repayment and in your loan statement.
Timing of Late payments
Late payment fees (“LPF”), including late payment interest and any applicable collection fee under Clause 7.3, shall be charged only after the default period specified in your loan agreement (being two (2) days past due. Such fees shall apply effective from the beginning of the first default day, specifically at 00:00:01 on the day DPD 2 commences, and shall be limited to reasonable recovery expenses not exceeding the outstanding principal, in compliance with the in duplum rule and Central Bank of Kenya regulations. All applicable LPF will be notified to you via the App or SMS immediately upon application and reflected in your Account. The circumstances under which these fees may be imposed, including the default period and precise timing of application, are fully disclosed in your loan agreement and key information document under Clause 7.1, and may be subject to variation with at least thirty (30) days’ prior notice.
